# Orcarouter Model Picker Diagnosis

Session: 2026-08-18. User's Hermes Agent config had orcarouter set up as a bare custom endpoint (inline `model.provider: custom` + `model.base_url`). The `/model` picker showed no orcarouter option.

## Root Cause

Config was:

```yaml
model:
  default: orcarouter/auto
  provider: custom
  base_url: https://api.orcarouter.ai/v1
```

This is the "bare custom" form. The `/model` picker inventory (`hermes_cli/inventory.py` → `build_models_payload` → `list_authenticated_providers`) only enumerates providers from:

- `providers:` dict (new-style, keyed by provider name)
- `custom_providers:` list (legacy)

A bare `provider: custom` with inline `base_url` on the `model:` section is NOT in either collection, so it never appears in the picker.

## What Still Works

The runtime provider resolution (`runtime_provider.py:_get_named_custom_provider`) falls back to the bare custom trust path when no named entry matches — it uses `model.base_url` directly. So `/model qwen3.8-27b-free` (typing the model name directly) should still switch the model while keeping the orcarouter base_url. But you can't browse available models via the picker.

## Fix Applied Conceptually

Add to `providers:`:

```yaml
providers:
  orcarouter:
    api: https://api.orcarouter.ai/v1
```

And change model section to:

```yaml
model:
  default: orcarouter/auto
  provider: orcarouter
```

This makes orcarouter appear in the `/model` picker with its discovered models.

## Available Models

To discover what models orcarouter actually serves, probe its `/v1/models` endpoint:

```bash
curl -s https://api.orcarouter.ai/v1/models | python3 -m json.tool
```

The user confirmed using free models like `qwen3.8-27b-free` — this is the model name to use with `/model <name>` if staying on the bare custom config.

## Code References

- `hermes_cli/inventory.py:load_picker_context()` — builds the ConfigContext from disk config; bare custom model.base_url is read but the provider is not added to `user_providers` or `custom_providers`
- `hermes_cli/inventory.py:build_models_payload()` — calls `list_authenticated_providers()` which only emits rows for providers in `user_providers` / `custom_providers`
- `hermes_cli/model_switch.py:_bare_custom_provider_def()` — constructs a ProviderDef for bare custom endpoints at switch time, but this is not used by the picker inventory path
- `hermes_cli/runtime_provider.py:_get_named_custom_provider()` — scans `providers:` then `custom_providers:`; falls through to bare custom when no match
